WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.925
What Webb saw in the Tarantula.

00:02.721 --> 00:05.076
This picture is the Webb telescope's own.

00:05.513 --> 00:10.806
It is made in infrared light, which no eye can see, so every colour in it is chosen.

00:11.318 --> 00:18.463
Infrared passes through dust, and here it shows tens of thousands of young stars that no telescope had seen before.

00:19.029 --> 00:24.414
The picture is 340 light-years across, in a small galaxy beside ours.
